opencl: soft_max of a fully masked row gives 0
Fold-into: upstream/ggml-opencl

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 plus every patch of the series before this one.

When each value of a SOFT_MAX row and the sink are -inf, the row maximum is
-inf, and the four soft_max kernels compute exp(-inf - (-inf)), which is NaN,
in each column. The CPU backend gives 0 for such a row (patches/fuzz-ops/0006).
The app graphs do not reach this condition: their masks have no fully masked
row.

This patch writes 0 into each column of such a row after the reduction of the
maximum, in soft_max_f32, soft_max_f16, soft_max_4_f32 and soft_max_4_f16.
test_soft_max_masked_row of test-backend-ops tests the change.

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-opencl/kernels/softmax_4_f16.cl b/ggml/src/ggml-opencl/kernels/softmax_4_f16.cl
index 571d165..c0b8174 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-opencl/kernels/softmax_4_f16.cl
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-opencl/kernels/softmax_4_f16.cl
@@ -87,6 +87,16 @@ kernel void kernel_soft_max_4_f16(
 
     const float max = sub_group_reduce_max(lmax);
 
+    // A fully masked row (each value and the sink are -inf) has no finite value. Its result is 0 in
+    // each column, as on the CPU, and not the NaN of exp(-inf - (-inf)). max comes from
+    // sub_group_reduce_max, thus each work item of the row takes the same branch.
+    if (max == -INFINITY) {
+        for (int i00 = get_local_id(0); i00 < ne00/4; i00 += get_local_size(0)) {
+            pdst4[i00] = 0.0f;
+        }
+        return;
+    }
+
     // parallel sum
     float4 lsum4 = 0.0f;
     for (int i00 = get_local_id(0); i00 < ne00/4; i00 += get_local_size(0)) {
